# Tracked websites
#
# One source per line: `<type> | <url>` with an optional `| note` at the end.
#   type = rss   → an RSS/Atom feed URL (preferred; cheap + reliable)
#   type = site  → a homepage/listing page the agent crawls for new article links
# Blank lines and `#` comments are ignored.
#
# SETUP: copy this file to `websites.md` and replace the entries below (or put your
# real websites.md in $AGENT_STATE_DIR/config/ if you keep state in a separate repo):
#
#   cp config/websites.md.example config/websites.md
#
# TIP: `python -m src.main add-site <url>` visits a site, auto-detects its RSS feed
# (falling back to `site` if none), and appends the right line here for you.

# RSS feeds (preferred)
rss  | https://www.letsrun.com/feed/
rss  | https://www.outsideonline.com/rss/

# Raw sites (no RSS; the agent crawls the homepage/listing for new article links,
# capped per run and rate-limited). Route region-specific sites through a proxy if
# they geo-block datacenter IPs — see OUTBOUND_PROXY_URL in .env.
site | https://www.example-athletics.org/news
